"Internal Use" means use of the Software by You for the internal operations
of Your own organization, including use by Your employees, contractors, and
other persons acting on Your behalf, provided that the Software is not
operated or made available for the purpose of providing a FlareMail-based
service to an unrelated third party.

"Third Party" means any individual or legal entity other than You and
persons acting on Your behalf.

"Deployment Service" means a service provided to a Third Party for
compensation, directly or indirectly, consisting substantially of
installing, configuring, provisioning, integrating, or deploying the
Software for that Third Party, whether on infrastructure owned by the
Third Party, Your infrastructure, or infrastructure controlled by another
party.

"Managed Service" means a service provided to a Third Party for
compensation, directly or indirectly, consisting substantially of hosting,
operating, administering, monitoring, maintaining, updating, or otherwise
managing the Software for that Third Party.

"Commercial Service" means a Deployment Service or a Managed Service.

"Independently Distinct Work" means a derivative work based on the Software
that has undergone substantial modifications such that, considered as a
whole, it is no longer recognizable as FlareMail to a reasonable person
familiar with the Software. Cosmetic changes, rebranding alone,
configuration, packaging, localization, dependency updates, theme or UI
skinning, or minor feature additions do not make a work Independently
Distinct. Removing FlareMail trademarks, logos, or product names without
substantial functional and architectural change does not make a work
Independently Distinct.

"Authorized Provider" means the Licensor or a Third Party that has received
explicit written authorization from the Licensor to provide Deployment
Services or Managed Services involving the Software.

