is not an Independently Distinct Work.

Without limiting the foregoing, You may not, for compensation or other
commercial consideration:

  (a) deploy or install the Software for a Third Party;
  (b) configure or provision the Software for a Third Party as a paid
      deployment engagement;
  (c) host the Software on behalf of a Third Party;
  (d) operate or administer the Software on behalf of a Third Party;
  (e) provide ongoing maintenance or management of a Third Party's
      FlareMail deployment as a service; or
  (f) provide a managed, hosted, or outsourced version of the Software to
      a Third Party.

This restriction applies to the Software and to modified, integrated,
repackaged, or rebranded versions that remain recognizable as FlareMail,
including when provided under a different service name.

Exception. Section 4 does not prohibit You from providing Commercial
Services that involve only an Independently Distinct Work. Such services
remain subject to Section 8 (Trademarks and Branding): You must not use
FlareMail marks or imply that the Independently Distinct Work or Your
service is FlareMail or is provided by the Licensor.

Calling a prohibited Commercial Service "consulting," "technical
assistance," "implementation," "integration," "DevOps," "hosting,"
"support," "maintenance," "managed infrastructure," or another similar
term does not remove the restriction where the substance of the service is
a Deployment Service or Managed Service involving the Software or a
modified version that is not an Independently Distinct Work.

